    "narrative": "Heading into today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Freeman** (71.23) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) lead the LawDog offense as our primary point-earners. **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a neutral platoon matchup against a soft lefty, but his real value is boosted by a favorable park factor and a premium #2 hole placement. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** is primed for a high-output day; his 5.17 xERA matchup against Kochanowicz is the softest on the board, and his high xwOBA suggests he is due for significant production. **Matt Chapman** (67.18), **Luis Arraez** (66.21), and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (65.93) round out the core, with **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert** all benefiting from a secondary tactical advantage: the slow delivery of Gordon, which elevates their stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given the league's scarcity of speed.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Taylor Ward** (49.55) and **Bryson Stott** (48.87) on the bench. Both hovered near the 50-point threshold, but ultimately, they were squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-ceiling options against the favorable pitching matchups we targeted. While **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive park factor, he is suppressed by a difficult SP xERA matchup, causing him to fall below the efficiency of players like **Lawrence Butler** (65.13), who draws a much more favorable matchup against Warren. We are exercising caution with **Daulton Varsho** (57.54), whose score is dampened by a sub-4.00 xERA opponent and an elite hold rating on the pitcher that threatens his SB utility. With **Cal Raleigh** sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily into the current efficiency of our active core, keeping a close eye on the weather and late-inning lineup shifts to ensure we don't bleed plate appearances while chasing category gains.",
